  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[2,5],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(2)$ and $f(5).$\n\nSince $f(2)=8$ and $f(5)=29,$ we must have \n$k\\in [8,29].$\n\nAmong the given options, only $k=10$ belongs to the interval $[8,29].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14197806/assets/14acd67d0b773864d39aaafcc6b41c9d8f3f10317b5e3f4584711baf157f346d.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
